 "critic": "The strongest generated cues were interchangeable full names, fixed reward formulas, abrupt shifts from third-person summaries to first-person speech, and repeated menus of three solutions. Several explanations felt attached after the event: an unfamiliar thief supposedly proves sponsorship, or an outsider thief supposedly requires an outsider investigator. Injury preventing paid work and recurring protection fees supplied convincing causes even when the wording felt templated. Ivo's refusal, deadline, threatened escalation, and emerging stallholder resistance formed the clearest connected situation. The repeated clinic, stolen-bag, crew-fight, and Friday-fee structures often supplied actions more specifically than they supplied people or motives.",
 "sheet": 1
